      "question": "In what ways has the structure of duty exemptions evolved from discretionary measures to the current sectoral approach?",
      "answer": "The structure evolved from general discretionary exemptions used in earlier years to a complex, table-based system for specific raw materials and capital goods, such as the multi-table structure introduced in SRO 148/2016. By 2024, this progressed further into a framework of diverse sectoral duty exemptions based on ad valorem thresholds, eventually shifting toward full sectoral exemptions as indicated by SRO 249/2024.",
